Commitment of case of Court of Session when offence is triable exclusively by it :--When in a case instituted on a police report or otherwise the accused appears or is brought before the Magistrate and it appears to the Magistrate that the offence is triable exclusively by the Court of Session, he shall--
(a) commit, after complying with the provisions of
Section 207
Section 208
as the case may be, the case to the Court of Session, and subject to the provisions of this Code relating to bail, remand the accused to custody until such commitment had been made;
(b) subject to the provisions of this Code relating to bail remand the accused to custody during, and until the conclusion of, the trial;
(c) send to that Court the record of the case and the documents and articles, if any, which are to be produced in evidence;
(d) notify the Public Prosecutor of the commitment of the case of the Court of Session."
